1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,920
Hello everyone, this is Ria!

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:08,290
Here is a calendar.

3
00:00:08,290 --> 00:00:09,770
Calendar

4
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:17,160
What are Saturday and Sunday in Korean?

5
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:20,540
Saturday and Sunday

6
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,150
Yes, they are the weekend!

7
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:24,530
Weekend

8
00:00:24,530 --> 00:00:32,290
Then, what are Monday through Friday in Korean?

9
00:00:32,290 --> 00:00:33,730
Yes, that's right.

10
00:00:33,730 --> 00:00:36,340
They are called weekdays.

11
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,870
Weekdays

12
00:00:37,870 --> 00:00:41,720
Do you like weekdays?

13
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:44,980
Or do you like weekends?

14
00:00:44,980 --> 00:00:52,470
Is there anyone here who answered "I like weekdays more!"?

15
00:00:52,470 --> 00:00:56,540
Probably not.

16
00:00:56,540 --> 00:01:06,210
Usually, Korean companies start work at 9 in the morning.

17
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:07,850
9 o'clock

18
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:13,400
They start at 9 and finish at 6.

19
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:20,760
Start at 9 in the morning and finish at 6 in the evening.

20
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:31,540
On Sunday night, when the weekend ends, many Koreans say this:

21
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:35,230
Ah, I don't want to go to work...

22
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:38,620
I really don't want to go to work.

23
00:01:38,620 --> 00:01:44,090
"Going to work" means going to the company to work.

24
00:01:44,090 --> 00:01:45,770
Going to work

25
00:01:45,770 --> 00:01:47,910
To go to work.

26
00:01:47,910 --> 00:01:54,600
Especially on Mondays, everyone hates going to work.

27
00:01:54,600 --> 00:02:03,290
If you take the subway on Monday morning, everyone's expression is not good.

28
00:02:03,290 --> 00:02:06,180
Their expressions are not good.

29
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:13,440
So in Korean, there is a word called "Monday sickness."

30
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,520
Monday sickness

31
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:22,200
The word "sickness" is originally used when your body is sick.

32
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,120
When your body is sick

33
00:02:24,120 --> 00:02:32,520
But here, it's a combined word of "Monday" (wol-yo) and "sickness" (byeong).

34
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,010
Combined word

35
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:37,010
So what does it mean?

36
00:02:37,010 --> 00:02:44,180
It means it's hard like you're sick on Monday, like you caught a disease.

37
00:02:44,180 --> 00:02:45,920
It's hard.

38
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:49,750
It's said jokingly like this.

39
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:56,370
Do you remember the word we learned in the old podcast?

40
00:02:56,370 --> 00:03:04,500
When talking about iPhones, we learned the word "Apple sickness."

41
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:14,100
Interestingly, in the US, they also use this word in English.

42
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:18,550
Then how about Monday sickness, everyone?

43
00:03:18,550 --> 00:03:24,350
Does your language have a word like this?

44
00:03:24,350 --> 00:03:29,460
If you get through Monday well, it becomes Friday.

45
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:30,820
Friday

46
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:33,400
Finally, Friday

47
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:39,760
If you work just one more day, you can rest the next day.

48
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:44,380
Finally, you can rest the next day.

49
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:48,080
The next day is the weekend.

50
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:49,340
Weekend

51
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:54,130
So everyone waits only for Friday.

52
00:03:54,130 --> 00:04:00,390
They wait to leave work quickly on Friday.

53
00:04:00,390 --> 00:04:01,980
Leaving work

54
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:04,020
To leave work.

55
00:04:04,020 --> 00:04:11,350
Leaving work means finishing work and leaving the company.

56
00:04:11,350 --> 00:04:13,850
Work is finished.

57
00:04:13,850 --> 00:04:16,550
And then you go home.

58
00:04:16,550 --> 00:04:19,280
This is leaving work.

59
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:26,630
But do Korean people go home after leaving work?

60
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:37,330
If they are really tired, some go home, but most go out to have fun.

61
00:04:37,330 --> 00:04:42,230
In Korean, there is a word called "Bulgeum."

62
00:04:42,230 --> 00:04:46,430
Burning Friday = Bulgeum

63
00:04:46,430 --> 00:04:53,340
On Bulgeum, after leaving work, many people go out to have fun.

64
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:54,830
Go out to have fun.

65
00:04:54,830 --> 00:05:06,450
If you look around the streets of Seoul from Friday evening, it's very crowded.

66
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:09,620
What does "bukkeok-bukkeok" mean?

67
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:18,580
"Bukkeok-bukkeok" means there are so many people that it feels noisy and crowded.

68
00:05:18,580 --> 00:05:25,490
On Friday, wherever you go in Seoul, there are many people.

69
00:05:25,490 --> 00:05:31,860
There are many places to have fun in Seoul on Bulgeum.

70
00:05:31,860 --> 00:05:43,680
There are many places to have fun, but I usually go to Gangnam or a place called Euljiro on Bulgeum.

71
00:05:43,680 --> 00:05:47,260
Gangnam and Euljiro in Korea.

72
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:50,140
These are places I like.

73
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:56,170
But these two places have very different vibes.

74
00:05:56,170 --> 00:06:03,860
But I want to recommend the place called Euljiro to you all.

75
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:06,070
I want to recommend it.

76
00:06:06,070 --> 00:06:15,850
In Seoul's Euljiro, you can eat outside until late at night.

77
00:06:15,850 --> 00:06:17,510
Outside

78
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:22,080
I like eating outside.

79
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:27,450
You can eat outside when the weather is nice.

80
00:06:27,450 --> 00:06:30,810
The atmosphere is really good.

81
00:06:30,810 --> 00:06:38,680
I will tell you more about Seoul later.

82
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:47,020
But I traveled in Japan for a long time.

83
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:54,640
When I was in Japan, I met friends and had fun on Friday nights.

84
00:06:54,640 --> 00:07:00,140
I met friends and had fun on Friday nights.

85
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:02,900
Japan's Bulgeum

86
00:07:02,900 --> 00:07:07,320
I went out to enjoy Japan's Bulgeum.

87
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:16,880
But when I went out on Friday night, there were so many people.

88
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:21,270
It was very similar to Korea.

89
00:07:21,270 --> 00:07:23,350
It was similar.

90
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:29,690
There were many people on the streets and it was very crowded.

91
00:07:29,690 --> 00:07:32,250
It was very crowded.

92
00:07:32,250 --> 00:07:42,450
As expected! As expected! It seems that Bulgeum is loved not only by Koreans but by everyone.

93
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:49,530
But I traveled to Japan with a Swiss friend.

94
00:07:49,530 --> 00:07:53,720
But that Swiss friend was very surprised.

95
00:07:53,720 --> 00:08:05,490
My Swiss friend told me that in Switzerland, there aren't this many people on Friday nights.

96
00:08:05,490 --> 00:08:09,720
There aren't this many people.

97
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:15,220
How is the Bulgeum atmosphere in your country?

98
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:21,430
Is it very crowded and bustling like in Korea and Japan?

99
00:08:21,430 --> 00:08:25,590
Or is it a bit quiet?

100
00:08:25,590 --> 00:08:33,230
Hmm... Now I will tell you what I do on weekdays.

101
00:08:33,230 --> 00:08:34,360
Weekdays

102
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:37,750
Mon Tue Wed Thu Fri = weekdays

103
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:44,880
Actually, I work both on weekdays and weekends.

104
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:52,080
I work without distinguishing between weekdays and weekends.

105
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:55,410
I work without distinguishing.

106
00:08:55,410 --> 00:09:06,450
So honestly, Bulgeum doesn't feel that special to me.

107
00:09:06,450 --> 00:09:09,900
It doesn't feel that special.

108
00:09:09,900 --> 00:09:22,780
No matter the day, when all the work is done, that's Bulgeum for me.

109
00:09:22,780 --> 00:09:25,970
It feels like Bulgeum.

110
00:09:25,970 --> 00:09:30,090
A feeling of liberation!

111
00:09:30,090 --> 00:09:39,570
There might be people like me whose work is not very regular.

112
00:09:39,570 --> 00:09:43,730
There might be people whose work is not regular.

113
00:09:43,730 --> 00:09:58,360
Work being regular means the time is fixed from Monday to Friday, 9 to 6.

114
00:09:58,360 --> 00:10:04,380
When the time is fixed, we say it's "regular."

115
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:15,420
Anyway, my work is not regular, so sometimes it's hard, but there are many good times too.

116
00:10:15,420 --> 00:10:19,090
I don't have Monday sickness either.

117
00:10:19,090 --> 00:10:20,950
How about you?

118
00:10:20,950 --> 00:10:24,550
Are you waiting for Bulgeum?

119
00:10:24,550 --> 00:10:29,860
Or do you have a favorite day of the week?

120
00:10:29,860 --> 00:10:35,700
Please definitely tell me what you do on Bulgeum in your country.

121
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:41,720
Also, please definitely tell me your favorite day in the comments!

122
00:10:41,720 --> 00:10:49,810
If you want to study more fun with me, please click this link too.

123
00:10:49,810 --> 00:10:55,980
Thank you so much for listening to my podcast today.

124
00:10:55,980 --> 00:11:00,460
See you next time with a more fun podcast!

125
00:11:00,460 --> 00:11:07,900
Have a good day on weekdays and weekends! Bye :)
